# Cloudflare Pages — SPA fallback. Every go_router path (/register, /family,
# /premium/retorno, the invitation and recovery links) is a client-side route:
# without this rule a reload or a deep link is a 404 served by the CDN before
# the app ever boots. Static files that exist are still served as themselves —
# this is the same single rule the Blazor PWA has always shipped.
# The legal pages the BLAZOR app served at this host, and which this app does
# not have (lote 4: one copy of the text, opened in the browser). The app
# itself now links straight to the landing, but every link already out there —
# in an e-mail, a bookmark, the old client — still names these paths, and after
# the domain move they would land here. First match wins, so these come BEFORE
# the SPA fallback below.
/privacy   https://entrelares.app/privacidade  301
/terms     https://entrelares.app/termos       301

/*  /index.html  200
